WEBVTT

00:00:05.700 --> 00:00:06.700
Aargh!

00:00:10.940 --> 00:00:12.540
(MUFFLED CRY)

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.900
Come on, Finn! It's now or never!

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:22.340
Hold on!

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:28.860
MATER: By the time you read this, I will
be safely on an airplane flying home.

00:00:29.260 --> 00:00:30.940
I'm so sorry for what I did.

00:00:31.020 --> 00:00:34.100
McQUEEN: "I don't want to be
the cause of you losing any more races.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:37.740
"I want you to go prove to the world
what I already know.

00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:41.220
"That you are the greatest race car
in the whole wide world.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.740
"Your best friend, Mater."

00:00:43.820 --> 00:00:45.820
-I didn't really want him to leave.
-(SOBS)

00:00:45.900 --> 00:00:48.220
Wait, there's more here.

00:00:48.380 --> 00:00:51.060
"PS. Please tell the hotel

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:53.380
"I didn't mean to order that movie.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:58.140
"I thought it was just a preview
and I didn't realize I was paying for it.

00:00:58.220 --> 00:01:01.220
"PPS. That's funny right there. PP."

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:04.180
There are a few more pages
of PS's here.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:07.820
Well, at least I know
if he's at home, he'll be safe.

00:01:09.980 --> 00:01:11.900
FINN: That's how I like to start the day.

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:14.660
You never feel more alive
than when you're almost dead.

00:01:14.740 --> 00:01:16.780
Yeah.
I hope that device didn't fall off.

00:01:16.860 --> 00:01:18.100
Whoa!

00:01:18.220 --> 00:01:20.860
That's the closest I ever been
to missin' my flight.

00:01:20.940 --> 00:01:22.700
That was... Oh!

00:01:23.260 --> 00:01:26.420
-Still in one piece? Great.
-MATER: I've got to go to a doctor.

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.940
I get these sharp pains
in my undercarriage.

00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:32.220
-Downloading the photo now.
-Let me introduce you two.

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:34.260
This here is Finn McSomethin'
or other.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.260
He's a first-class VIP
airport whatchamacallit.

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:40.580
And, Finn, this here is my date.

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.380
I never did get your name.

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:45.620
Oh, yes, sorry. It's Shiftwell.
Holley Shiftwell.

00:01:45.700 --> 00:01:47.100
It's Shiftwell. Holley...

00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:51.340
Finally.
Time to see who's behind all this.

00:01:52.020 --> 00:01:53.860
What is this?

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:56.660
That's one of the worst engines
ever made.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:01.460
It's an old aluminum V8 with a Lucas
electrical system and Whitworth bolts.

00:02:01.580 --> 00:02:04.780
Shoot, them Whitworth bolts is a pain,
tell you what.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:06.620
Them ain't metric, they ain't inches.

00:02:06.700 --> 00:02:09.420
Yes, OK, but whose engine is this?

00:02:09.460 --> 00:02:12.060
It's kinda hard to tell from this picture,
ain't it?

00:02:12.140 --> 00:02:13.660
-But you took it.
-Holley.

00:02:13.780 --> 00:02:15.820
Oh. Right! Yes, of course.

00:02:15.820 --> 00:02:18.980
A good agent gets what he can,
then gets out before he's killed.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:22.180
Agent? You mean, like,
insurance agent? Like...

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:26.660
(SINGING) Like a good neighbor,
Mater is there!

00:02:26.860 --> 00:02:29.900
Wait! You mean secret agents!
You guys is spies!

00:02:29.980 --> 00:02:33.100
In how many makes and models
did this type of engine appear?

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:36.740
It was standard in seven models
over a 12-year period.

00:02:36.820 --> 00:02:40.220
At least 35,000 cars were made
with this engine.

00:02:40.340 --> 00:02:42.500
-You're purty.
-Yes, thank you.

00:02:42.660 --> 00:02:45.820
-And so nice.
-Just pay attention.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:48.340
FINN: This seems like a dead end.

00:02:49.220 --> 00:02:53.020
If there was something in the photo that
could narrow this down, I'd be happier.

00:02:53.100 --> 00:02:55.900
You might not be happy,
but I bet this feller is.

00:02:55.980 --> 00:02:58.300
See how he's had most of his parts
replaced?

00:02:58.340 --> 00:03:00.260
And see all them boxes over there?

00:03:00.340 --> 00:03:03.180
Them's all original parts.
They ain't easy to come by.

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:06.180
-Rare parts?
-That's something we can track.

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:08.020
Exactly.

00:03:08.100 --> 00:03:10.940
Well done, Mater.
I would never have seen that.

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:14.740
I know of a black-market parts dealer
in Paris, a treacherous lowlife,

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:18.460
but he's the only car in the world
who can tell us whose engine this is.

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:22.220
What would you say to setting up
an informal task force on this one?

00:03:22.300 --> 00:03:23.380
Wait. What?

00:03:23.460 --> 00:03:25.660
You obviously have experience
in the field.

00:03:25.700 --> 00:03:27.980
Yeah, I live right next to one.

00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:30.140
I don't know.

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:33.060
I ain't exactly been much help
to anybody recently.

00:03:33.140 --> 00:03:35.260
You're helping me.
Please, Mater.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.500
Well... Okay.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:39.700
But you know
I'm just a tow truck, right?

00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:43.100
Right. And I'm just
in the import-export business.

00:03:43.260 --> 00:03:44.900
-Siddeley?
-Yes, Finn?

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:46.460
Paris. Tout de suite.

00:03:46.540 --> 00:03:49.140
Yeah, two of them sweets for me,
too, Sid.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:51.180
I always wanted to be a spy.

00:03:51.260 --> 00:03:52.900
Really? Me, too.

00:03:52.980 --> 00:03:56.020
-Afterburners, sir?
-Is there any other way?

00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.220
(TOOTING AND SHOUTING)

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:17.900
Ha ha ha!

00:04:26.740 --> 00:04:28.620
FINN: Once we're inside, stay close.

00:04:28.780 --> 00:04:32.060
Don't bother checking VIN numbers.
They're all dodgy here.

00:04:32.140 --> 00:04:33.420
Got it.

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:35.420
Don't talk to anyone,
don't look at anyone,

00:04:35.580 --> 00:04:38.460
and absolutely, positively no idling.
Are we clear?

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:40.380
Yes. No idling. Yes, sir.

00:04:41.220 --> 00:04:43.100
-Mater?
-Yeah, Finn?

00:04:43.180 --> 00:04:46.420
-We're not here to go shopping.
-Shoppin'? What do you mean?

00:04:46.460 --> 00:04:48.380
Why would I...

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:49.940
Dad-gum.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:53.020
-Part for sales, monsieur.
-Monsieur, part for sale.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:55.100
They got everything here. No!

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:57.580
Look at them hoods!
I could use a hood.

00:04:57.620 --> 00:04:59.340
Sorry, fellers. I gotta go!

00:05:01.460 --> 00:05:04.300
Wow. Whoa. He-he!

00:05:04.900 --> 00:05:06.900
Do what?

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:10.620
Excuse me. What are you selling?

00:05:10.780 --> 00:05:12.460
Headlights, monsieur, headlights?

00:05:12.620 --> 00:05:14.340
-What in the...?
-Two for one.

00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:16.020
-I give you good price!
-I'm good!

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:19.980
(CARS SPEAKING IN FRENCH)

00:05:20.900 --> 00:05:24.140
-FINN: There you are.
-There is some great bargains here.

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:26.220
-Mater, get back!
-Imbécile!

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:34.820
Hey, wait for me!

